### Python back-port (`code/cymatics.py`, additive only — v1 behavior unchanged)
- `lorentzian_superposition(modes, f_drive, gamma=None)` — normalized
  Lorentzian weights; γ=0 clamped to 1e-6 (never NaN), γ<0 raises, f=0 legal.
- `bessel_derivative_zeros(n_max, m_max)` / `bessel_derivative_zero(n, m)` —
  free-rim zero table (J' zeros) via `scipy.special.jnp_zeros` in its
  practical range (n≤100, m≤20) + brentq fallback on `scipy.special.jvp`.
- `frequency_membrane_free(n, m, R, c)` = z'_{n,m}·c/(2πR) — free-rim twin
  of `frequency_membrane` (same scaling laws, resonator-independent ratios).

### v2 stress tests (`code/test_cymatics.py`, +7 tests → 38 total)
Lorentzian peak sanity (on-peak dominance, off-peak suppression) and edge
cases (γ→0 clamp, f=0, γ<0 rejection, bad modes); free-rim zeros monotonic
in m and n≥1, A&S spot values, J'₀=−J₁ identity, scipy consistency; free-rim
frequency ratio/scaling/guard rails; extreme modes n=100 exact + n=101
fallback; membrane pattern vs analytic J_n(z·r/R)·cos(nθ+φ) parity; JS↔Python
cross-validation via node (Bessel zeros both rims, Lorentzian weights,
sand-sim determinism, ladder anchors; skipped cleanly if node absent).

### Honesty convention (adopted from Open Sync)
Frequency does NOT determine a real plate pattern — only idealized declared
virtual plates map Hz→modes (`CYM.HONESTY_NOTE`, chladni.ts header note).
UI-facing content keeps the 'physics'/'art' label contract: 'physics' =
eigenmode/Lorentzian simulation on a declared plate; 'art' = cultural
frequency choices (e.g. Solfeggio) with no physical claim.

